keywords:
  - time-varying media
  - temporal metamaterials
  - Rozanov bound
  - epsilon-near-zero
  - indium tin oxide
  - FDTD
  - two-temperature model
abstract: >-
  Material models of indium tin oxide, a one-dimensional FDTD at a fixed angle
  of incidence for planar stacks of time-varying Drude media, a two-temperature
  model of the pumped film, the studies that test chirp-matched temporal
  absorption against the Rozanov bound of non-magnetic static absorbers, and
  the scripts that derive the figures and tables of the paper from the stored
  results.
